The same eleven types as the firing archive, declared the same way, each handed to a
declaration of the target whose parameter is typed as the value's own type instead of
to its destination. Nothing in this archive flows into reflection, an encoder, a
template engine, a scan, the sort interface or a logging call, nothing crosses out of
the analysis through a parameter typed as an interface, and the one type converted to
the log-value interface reaches the class by that conversion no more than the others,
so the class records nothing. One value reaches a parameter typed as an interface
carrying a map of pointers, which is no struct value and no pointer to one.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/flow

go 1.27.1
-- json.go --
package flow

// JSONPayload reaches no encoder.
type JSONPayload struct {
	Name   string `json:"name"`
	Extra  int
	secret string `json:"secret"`
}

// Describe is exported.
func (p JSONPayload) Describe() string { return p.Name }

func (p JSONPayload) hidden() int { return p.Extra }

// StoreJSON hands a value to a declaration of the target typed as the value's own type.
func StoreJSON(p JSONPayload) { keptJSONPayload = p }

// keptJSONPayload is where the value goes, which crosses no boundary of the analysis.
var keptJSONPayload JSONPayload
